<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Geist, as the widget's typeface.

    Android ships no Geist — its default is Roboto — so unlike the CJK faces (which the system does
    have, and which index.css deliberately leaves to it) this one has to be carried. It is the same
    typeface the WebView already renders from woff2 inside this APK; `res/font` cannot read woff2, so
    this is that font again as a TTF. The latin subset only: the widget's own strings are Latin, and
    a habit named in Japanese falls through Android's per-glyph fallback to system Noto, which is the
    same rendering the app's :lang() stack picks for it.

    One file, two weights. Geist is variable (wght 100-900, default 400), so the bold entry asks the
    same file for 700 rather than shipping a second cut. `fontVariationSettings` is API 26+; below
    that the entry is ignored and the platform synthesises bold from the 400 instance, which is what
    would have happened anyway without this file.
-->
<font-family xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <font
        android:fontStyle="normal"
        android:fontWeight="400"
        android:fontVariationSettings="'wght' 400"
        android:font="@font/geist" />
    <font
        android:fontStyle="normal"
        android:fontWeight="500"
        android:fontVariationSettings="'wght' 500"
        android:font="@font/geist" />
    <font
        android:fontStyle="normal"
        android:fontWeight="700"
        android:fontVariationSettings="'wght' 700"
        android:font="@font/geist" />
</font-family>
